==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|de|Marke}}, from {{der|ru|fr|marque}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|ма́рка}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-марка.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|ма́рка|*|adj=ма́рочный|dim=ма́рочка}}

# [[stamp]] {{gl|small, adhesive paper document}}
#: {{coi|ru|[[почтовая марка|почто́вая '''ма́рка''']]|postage '''stamp'''}}
# [[brand]], [[make]]
#: {{syn|ru|бренд|tr=brɛnd}}
#: {{coi|ru|[[торговый|торго́вая]] '''ма́рка'''|[[trademark]]}}
# [[grade]], [[quality]] (of a product)
#: {{syn|ru|ка́чество|сорт}}
# {{lb|ru|slang}} [[LSD]], or [[tab]] of LSD
# [[mark#English:_unit_and_currency|mark]] {{gl|mostly historical unit of currency in various countries}}
#: {{coi|ru|[[немецкий|неме́цкая]] '''ма́рка'''|[[Deutsche Mark|Deutsche '''Mark''']]}}
#: {{coi|ru|[[финский|фи́нская]] '''ма́рка'''|Finnish '''[[markka]]'''}}
# {{lb|ru|historical}} [[mark#English:_unit_and_currency|mark]] {{gl|half-pound unit of weight mostly used for gold and silver}}
# {{lb|ru|historical}} [[march]], [[mark]] {{gl|medieval administrative unit used for borderlands}}
# {{lb|ru|historical}} [[chip]] or [[token]] used for payment in taverns or point-counting in games
#: {{syn|ru|жето́н|фи́шка}}
#: {{coi|ru|[[трактирный|тракти́рная]] '''ма́рка'''|tavern '''chip'''}}
#: {{coi|ru|[[игровой|игрова́я]] '''ма́рка'''|game '''token'''}}

